## Final Count

Each valid ordered triple contributes $N_p \cdot N_q \cdot N_r = (p-1)(q-1)(r-1)$, since every size-3 pattern has count $s-1$ for prime $s$.

By CRT, the total number of triples $(a,b,c) \in \{1,\ldots,pqr\}^3$ with seven distinct clearance levels is:

$$48 \cdot (p-1)(q-1)(r-1)$$

